#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
iris-talk — a spoken voice companion that watches your Hyprland desktop.

It closes the loop the existing `iris` voice layer left open:

    you speak  ->  STT (iris-comms /stt/transcribe)
              ->  gather context (active window, terminal cwd + git,
                  your live Claude Code session, a screenshot)
              ->  think  (Claude via `claude -p`, conversation kept with --resume)
              ->  iris-say (iris-comms /tts/stream) speaks the reply

Trigger model (phase 1): a single toggle. Tap the key (or click the waybar
eye) once to start listening, tap again to send + hear the reply. State is
mirrored to a waybar module so the eye shows idle / listening / thinking /
speaking.

Subcommands:
    iris-talk            toggle (start if idle, else stop+answer)  [default]
    iris-talk start      begin recording
    iris-talk stop       stop recording, answer
    iris-talk cancel     drop the in-progress recording, say nothing
    iris-talk waybar     print the waybar module JSON for the current state
    iris-talk reset      forget the conversation (start a fresh session)
    iris-talk --text "…" skip the mic; feed text straight to the brain (debug)

Reuses the iris-comms endpoints and API key already configured for iris-ptt.
"""
